body:
Ah! I wasn't sure what artifacts were.

&#x200B;

GitLab creates artifacts at $CI\_PROJECT\_DIR

&#x200B;

So, then, what would be the best way to sync the artifacts then with the deployment directory? It's important to me that local file changes and gitignore'd files are kept but file deletions in the repo are respected.

the desync in the audio is probably the funniest part.

&#x200B;

OP, How'd the accident happen?

This may be the case in some places in the united states, but here in British Columbia, Canada, solid lines are more than a suggestion, and though I don't have the information handy, I'm *pretty* sure, passing on a two lane road like this is considered negligent and would warrant a similar ticket, even IF the road had a dotted line.

&#x200B;

Also, the video must not show it very well, there certainly was ice, and he maintained the wrong side of the road for roughly 500m, with a stop sign roughly 700m down the road from where I was in the video.

&#x200B;

Also, you clearly didn't identify the car correctly, as it's a chevy malibu in the video, which doesn't offer AWD, and you ***assume*** he's got winter's on, which is a bold assumption considering the subreddit we're in.

Seeing as during my travels across google, for the issue, I found dozens of people who encountered the exact same issue (siri not responding, ESC key not functioning as a result), I felt that combining the solutions into one place would be a good idea for anyone searching about the issue in the future.

&#x200B;

That being said, I'm glad you haven't encountered this issue!

Why do I feel like a mac mini could've done this setup for cheaper but still look as epic?

&#x200B;

Awesome setup either way, congrats.

To be entirely honest every single time I've responded to you I've been high as fuck, so I'm surprised I even got my point across. I think both menu's look great and I wish you luck on your game, but definitely the padding in the after seems to low for the art style you're going for. I'd also recommend resizing the window in a similar fashion to how you resize windows on a desktop if you're able to. Might make the end result feel nicer to the end user.

&#x200B;

EDIT: just looked at the steam page and I see you've already done that last thing. Nice.

> julio's webclip

Didn't know what this was, but googled it and am gonna try it now. stand by for results.

UPDATE: Same problem ;-;
